# Local SSO for `make run-orbital`.
#
# Copy this file to `orbital.env` (gitignored) and fill in the client secret.
# The Makefile sources `deploy/local/orbital.env` when it exists — if it does
# not, orbital still runs and the password login still works, so a fresh clone
# needs no setup at all. This file only adds the "Sign in with Microsoft" button.
#
# These are NOT defaults in config.go on purpose: a tenant or client id baked in
# as a default silently points someone else's deployment at our identity
# provider. They are public identifiers, not secrets — the secret is the one
# blank line below.

# ── Armada dev tenant (replace both with your own to run against another IdP) ─
ORBITAL_OIDC_ISSUER_URL=https://login.microsoftonline.com/8f231c2a-9551-4b40-be17-5b24afe5e890/v2.0
ORBITAL_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=5fc832f6-843e-4207-93dd-b3c3a77c06f2

# ── The actual secret — never commit this file with a value here ─────────────
# Azure portal → App registrations → orbital → Certificates & secrets.
ORBITAL_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
